<LegalLayout 
  title="Cookie Policy" 
  description="Cookie Policy for Bangladesh Travel Guide: which cookies and similar technologies Google Analytics may set, and how to manage or block them."
  lastUpdated="October 25, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Cookie Policy explains what cookies and similar technologies may be used when you visit <a href="https://www.bangladeshtravelguide.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.bangladeshtravelguide.com</a>. It should be read with our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What Are Cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files stored on your device by your browser when you visit a website. Similar technologies, such as web beacons, pixels, and local storage, work in comparable ways. They are used to remember information, measure how a site is used, and track advertising and referrals.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Cookies Set by This Website</h2>
  <p>
    Bangladesh Travel Guide does not set its own cookies to store personal information or preferences. We do not use accounts, logins, or shopping carts. The cookies you may encounter on the site come from the third-party services below.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Third-Party Cookies and Technologies</h2>

  <h3>Analytics: Google Analytics</h3>
  <p>
    Google Analytics uses cookies, such as those beginning with <code>_ga</code>, to recognise a browser and compile reports on traffic and usage, including pages viewed, approximate location, and device type. We use these reports in aggregate to improve our guides. Cookie lifetimes are set by Google and are typically up to two years. See Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cookie information</a> and the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">opt-out browser add-on</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    We also use Google Search Console, which reports on how our pages perform in Google Search. It does not place cookies on visitors' devices through our pages.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How to Manage or Block Cookies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Browser settings:</strong> You can block, delete, or receive warnings about cookies in your browser's privacy settings. Blocking some cookies may change how ads and links behave.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> Install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">opt-out add-on</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Ad personalisation:</strong> Use your <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ad Center</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy tools:</strong> Private browsing, tracking protection, and content blockers can limit analytics, advertising, and affiliate tracking.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Browser help pages explain these steps: <a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chrome</a>, <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/kb/enhanced-tracking-protection-firefox-desktop" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firefox</a>, and <a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Safari</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Cookie Policy if the services we use change. The date at the top shows when it was last revised.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about cookies on this website, please use our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>. We aim to reply as soon as we reasonably can.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>